---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Tic-Tac-Toe Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Tic-Tac-Toe Easy, the iOS game."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/tic-tac-toe-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Tic-Tac-Toe Easy?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Tic-Tac-Toe%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

        <div class="space-y-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I start a game?</h3>
            <p>Open the app and tap any cell. You play X against the computer at Medium until you change it. Tap the arrow at the top right, or Play again when a game ends, to start over.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How hard is each level?</h3>
            <p>Easy takes a win when it sees one and otherwise plays anywhere. Medium also blocks your wins and plays its best move about half the time. Hard plays a perfect game: it never loses, so a draw against Hard is the best anyone can do.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can the computer go first?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Under Your mark, choose "O, go second" and the computer opens as X.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I play with a friend?</h3>
            <p>Choose Friend at the bottom of Play and pass the phone back and forth. X always goes first.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Why did my game start over?</h3>
            <p>Changing the opponent, the difficulty or your mark starts a new game. A game counts toward your scores only once it ends, so a game you leave unfinished isn't counted.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What counts as a streak?</h3>
            <p>Your streak is how many games in a row you've won at a level. A loss ends it; a draw leaves it as it is. Scores shows your current streak and your best one.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I reset my scores?</h3>
            <p>Open the menu, tap Settings, then Reset scores. This clears every win, loss, draw and streak, and it can't be undone.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I change the colors or the app icon?</h3>
            <p>Yes. In Settings, pick Light, Dark or System, and Graphite or Black after dark. Under Accent, choose one of eight colors. The accent draws the winning line and changes the app icon to match.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where is my data stored?</h3>
            <p>Your scores and settings stay on your iPhone. They're included in your iCloud or computer backup, so restoring a backup on a new iPhone brings them with you.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
